  _narratorPrompt: A breather. This one is pure nonsense and I adore it, so answer quickly. You must fight, bare handed, either one duck grown to the size of a horse, or a hundred horses shrunk to the size of ducks. Which do you take on.
  _choices:
  - _id: giant_duck
    _label: The giant duck
    _narratorReact: One enormous duck. You want a single foe you can look in the eye, even a preposterous one. There is something almost principled in that. Almost.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty:
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 38
    _profileImpact: []
  - _id: tiny_horses
    _label: The tiny horses
    _narratorReact: A hundred little horses. You would rather be swarmed by the many than face the one. A crowd fighter. Even here, playing the odds. That tells me a little.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty:
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 62
    _profileImpact: []
  _figuresBranded: 0
  _statsHeading: how others chose
  _crowdSafeFraction: 0.43
  _crowdThreshold: 0.5
  _thresholdLabel: the line
